                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_426">Oxford, Oxfordshire.
                        Balliol College (Domus de Balliolo)</orgName><p>‘Liber domus de Balliolo
                        ex legato Magistri Johannis Waltam subdecani ecclesie | Eboracensis quondam
                        socii predicte domus cuius anime propicietur deus Amen’ (fol. 1v)‘The
                        Balliol inventory-mark 28’ liber theologie is on 4.’ (Mynors, Balliol,
                        24)‘On 356v are three later notes of pledging: (a) Caucio [magistrorum,
                        perhaps Willelmi Saxton et Rogeri] Gowsell exposita in cista de Routhbery
                        pro quinque marcis vii solidis in festo sancti Vitalis martyris [et?]
                        Augustini apostoli Anglorum A.D. m.cccc.xviij et luat Saxton ; (b) Caucio
                        magistri Willelmi Saxton exposita in cista de Rowbery pro undecim marcis et
                        septem solidis in festo sancti Vitalis martiris A.D. m.cccc.xvii et habet
                        supplementum 2o fo. ‘disceret’ (?) et caveat et luat solus prefatus Saxton ;
                        (c) Caucio magistrorum Willelmi Saxton Roberti Forester et Rogeri Gowsell
                        exposita in cista de Rowbery pro quinque marcis (et septem solidis et ego
                        Saxton sic subscripsi added) in festo Martini in yeme A.D. m.cccc.xvo et
                        luat Saxton domus de Balliolo.’ (Mynors, Balliol, 24)</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">John de Waltham (d. 1384), fellow of
                     Balliol</provenance>
